> **Farzana says:** "The bow tie is the oval buyer's trap. I have seen buyers spend $15,000 on a 2ct oval with a certificate that looks perfect — then receive a stone with a bow tie so dark it ruins the face-up appearance. Every oval purchase needs a video. Not stock photography. A real video of the specific stone, rotating in natural light. That is not optional."

