## The Sparkle Split

The oval and emerald cut attract buyers with fundamentally different preferences. Neither is wrong. But conflating them leads to disappointment.

**Oval buyers want:**
- Maximum sparkle and fire from every angle
- A stone that looks lively and brilliant in all lighting
- A shape that hides clarity issues — VS2 is often eye-clean in an oval
- A color-tolerant stone — H in white gold looks white because the 58 facets break color into sparkle

**Emerald cut buyers want:**
- The hall-of-mirrors effect — slow, deep reflections through the long step facets
- A stone that reads sophisticated and architectural rather than flashy
- A shape where the quality shows — VVS or VS1 clarity, D–G color, visible in the open table
- A diamond that looks completely different from every brilliant cut ring in the room

This is The Sparkle Split. Oval gives you diamond as performance. Emerald cut gives you diamond as sculpture.

Most buyers who try both shapes in person know immediately which personality matches them. If you have not tried both in person, do it before buying — the difference is immediately apparent.

