## Face-Up Size: Which Looks Bigger?

Both shapes look larger than a round brilliant at the same carat weight. This is the most commonly cited reason buyers choose either shape.

The reason is the same for both: weight is distributed shallower and wider rather than deep. A 2ct round has roughly 8.1mm diameter. A 2ct oval stretches to approximately 10mm in length.

A 2ct emerald cut reaches approximately 8.5mm in length — narrower than an oval but with more rectangular coverage across the finger.

On the finger, the oval often appears larger because its length is visible on both sides of the band. The emerald cut appears more linear and architectural — it does not fan out to the sides but instead cuts cleanly across the finger.

**Approximate face-up dimensions by carat weight:**

