<tr><td>4.00ct</td><td>10.2mm</td><td>~13.5×9.0mm</td><td>~11.0×8.0mm</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

The oval typically has more total face-up area per carat because its brilliant cut allows for shallower depth. The emerald cut trades some face-up coverage for the step-cut's architectural look. Neither shape is dramatically larger than the other — both beat rounds at the same weight.

The choice between them on size alone is marginal; the aesthetic difference is enormous.

