## Clarity: What Each Shape Hides and Shows

This is the biggest practical difference between the two shapes. It affects your budget more than anything else in this comparison.

**Oval clarity floor: VS2 (GIA)**

The oval's 58 brilliant-cut facets scatter light aggressively. Inclusions in the body of the stone are fragmented and dispersed across the scintillation pattern. A GIA VS2 oval is almost always eye-clean.

Some VS2 ovals with inclusions at the edge or near the girdle are completely invisible to the naked eye.

SI1 in an oval is risky but not impossible — if the inclusion is positioned near the girdle and not in the center, SI1 can still be eye-clean. Many buyers choose SI1 oval diamonds successfully and save significant money versus VS2.

**Emerald cut clarity floor: VS1 (GIA)**

The emerald cut's open step-cut table is a window. There are no scattered facets to disguise inclusions. A feather crystal at the center of the table is visible at arm's length.

VS2 in an emerald cut sometimes shows — you must check the clarity plot to see where the inclusion sit. VS1 is the safe standard for an eye-clean result.

SI1 in an emerald cut almost always shows to the naked eye. It is not recommended under any circumstances.

**Clarity grade savings comparison:**

