The clarity difference has a real price impact. At 2ct natural, moving from VS2 to VS1 adds approximately $2,000–$4,000. Oval buyers who can buy VS2 (sometimes SI1) save that entire budget.

Emerald cut buyers must spend it.

---

## Color: How Each Shape Reads in Different Settings

**Oval color floor: H (GIA) in white gold**

The oval's brilliant-cut facets break color into sparkle. H-color in an oval looks white to most eyes in a white gold or platinum setting. Some buyers push to I-color in yellow gold with excellent results — the warm metal absorbs the warmth in the stone.

**Emerald cut color floor: G (GIA) in white gold**

The emerald cut's open, unbroken reflections show body color as warmth. An H-color emerald cut reads slightly warm in platinum. G is the comfortable minimum for a color-neutral appearance.

In yellow gold, G–J is acceptable since the warm metal offsets the warmer grades.

