## Proportions: What to Look for in Each Shape

**Oval proportions:**
- Length-to-width ratio: 1.30–1.50 for the classic elongated oval look. Below 1.30 looks round. Above 1.55 looks narrow and pin-like.
- Depth: 58–62% minimizes bow tie. Above 64% depth increases bow tie risk.
- Table: 53–63% is the preferred range.
- Polish and Symmetry: Excellent or Very Good minimum.

**Emerald cut proportions:**
- Length-to-width ratio: 1.30–1.50 for the classic elongated look. Below 1.30 looks square (approaches Asscher territory). Above 1.55 looks too narrow.
- Depth: 60–64% is the ideal range. Shallower stones (below 58%) window — they look transparent from above with no depth.
- Table: 61–69% is the preferred range.
- Polish and Symmetry: Excellent or Very Good. The long flat facets amplify any imperfection in symmetry.

**The L:W ratio effect on finger appearance:**

